1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Covered Material" means source code, object code, documentation, and
other copyrightable material to which a person or entity that owns or controls
the applicable copyright ("Licensor") has expressly applied this License.
Coverage is determined file-by-file and contribution-by-contribution. The
repository's LICENSE_SCOPE.md and notices may identify known coverage and
exclusions. No person grants rights that person does not own or control.

1.2 "Repository" means the repository that contains this License and any
release or archive expressly identified as originating from that repository.

1.3 "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising permissions under
this License. "Your" has a corresponding meaning. If You act for an employer,
school, team, organization, client, or other principal, "You" includes that
principal and all persons acting under its direction or control for the
relevant use.

1.4 "UMD Affiliate" means a currently enrolled student, faculty member, staff
member, or academic unit of the University of Maryland, College Park.

1.5 "Authorized UMD Team" means current UMD Affiliates acting for the
University of Maryland, College Park Terps Racing organization, including its
Electric Vehicle program and any formally recognized successor student vehicle
program, solely while acting for that UMD program.

1.6 "Competition Program" means any team, club, academic program, company,
organization, or coordinated group that participates in, prepares to
participate in, or materially supports a vehicle entered or intended to be
entered in Formula SAE, Formula Student, Formula Hybrid + Electric, Formula
Bharat, any SAE Collegiate Design Series vehicle event, or another
intercollegiate competition in which students design, build, simulate, test, or
race a vehicle and vehicle performance is evaluated.

1.7 "Competing Team" means any Competition Program other than the Authorized
UMD Team. It includes the program's current or prospective members, advisors,
faculty, sponsors, contractors, consultants, vendors, service providers, and
other persons acting for its benefit with respect to Competition Use.

1.8 "Competition Use" means using the Covered Material, a modified version,
or results produced by executing either, directly or indirectly, to design,
select, size, model, simulate, analyze, optimize, calibrate, tune, validate,
test, manufacture, inspect, control, operate, strategize for, train a driver
for, or otherwise improve a vehicle, subsystem, controller, software stack,
data pipeline, setup, or competition performance of a Competition Program.
Competition Use includes benchmarking against another vehicle or simulator,
processing competition telemetry, generating vehicle parameters, developing
torque control or torque vectoring, and providing any of those activities as
a service.

1.9 "Evaluation Use" means inspection, reproduction, execution, and private
modification solely to evaluate the Covered Material or its contributors for
employment, recruitment, academic review, code quality, security review, or
technical due diligence. Evaluation Use excludes Competition Use, production
deployment, commercial product development, and providing a hosted or managed
service.

1.10 "Educational Use" means coursework, teaching, independent study, and
noncommercial academic research by a UMD Affiliate. Educational Use excludes
Competition Use for a Competing Team, commercial product development, and any
use governed by a separate agreement that does not permit the use.

1.11 "Distribute" means to provide, publish, transmit, sublicense, sell,
lease, host for third-party access, or otherwise make a copy or modified
version available to another person or entity. Internal sharing expressly
permitted below is not Distribution.

1.12 "Scope Notice" means the version of `LICENSE_SCOPE.md` distributed with
the copy of Covered Material You received. A later change to that file does not
retroactively enlarge or reduce rights already granted for that copy unless
You and every applicable Licensor agree in a Signed Writing.

1.13 "Signed Writing" means a writing, including an electronic writing, that
clearly identifies the applicable Licensor, Covered Material, permission, and
recipient and bears that Licensor's manual or legally effective electronic
signature. A repository issue, pull request, comment, commit, email, chat
message, or oral statement is not a Signed Writing merely because it exists.

